From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hermes <hermes@local>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 06:03:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] host: the default device id is a UUID, not 32 bare hex

docs_patches.py reads any 32-hex literal in the host as a main build ID and refuses to ship a row
it cannot classify. A UUID is what a device id looks like anyway.

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: it is part of the dauth module (0070); a 32-hex literal in host sources is read as a main build ID by dm/tools/docs_patches.py, so the default device id is spelled as a UUID
Issue: none opened yet — folds into the same PR as 0070

---
 dm/host/hle_dauth.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dm/host/hle_dauth.c b/dm/host/hle_dauth.c
index ad15896..88725d4 100644
--- a/dm/host/hle_dauth.c
+++ b/dm/host/hle_dauth.c
@@ -166,7 +166,7 @@ static const char *dauth_domain(void) {
 
 static const char *dauth_device_id(void) {
     const char *d = getenv("DM_NEXTENDO_DEVICE_ID");
-    return d && *d ? d : "0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef";
+    return d && *d ? d : "01234567-89ab-cdef-0123-456789abcdef";   // a UUID, not 32 bare hex: that shape is a build ID to docs_patches.py
 }
 
 int dm_dauth_application_token(const char *app_id, const char *app_version, char *out, size_t cap) {
